# Dialogue layout
@scenario tutorial_lesson_15
@include /definitions/characters.vns
@label start
[mode dialogue standard]
[set ui.dialogueUi project]
[bg room]
[char ginger global on]
[set ui.dialogueFadeMs 160]
[stage clear]
[show ginger guide thoughtful]
ginger: See the space between my words and the edge of this box? Try making that margin a little wider.
ginger: Increase dialogueTextHorizontalPadding in config/ui/dialogue.layout. Compare two window sizes.
> Review question -> check
> Back to topics -> return_hub
@label check
ginger: Which setting changes text inset inside the panel?
> dialogueTextHorizontalPadding -> correct
> characterBaselineY -> retry
> Back to topics -> return_hub
@label retry
[show ginger guide confused]
ginger: Padding changes the inner margin. Character framing is independent. Give it another try.
[jump check]
@label correct
[show ginger guide normal]
ginger: Padding changes the inner margin. Character framing is independent.
> Back to topics -> return_hub
> Replay example -> start
@label return_hub
[if !tutorial_done_15]
[flag tutorial_done_15]
[inc tutorial_count]
[endif]
[stage clear]
[goto TutorialHub:topics_page_4]
